# Cutover runbook: {{ plan.source_cloud.value | upper }} → STACKIT

Run `{{ plan.run_id }}`. Generated from the migration plan; adjust to the
client's change process. The source environment stays untouched, which is the
rollback path.

## 1. Before the window

- Announce the maintenance window to the workload owners.
- Confirm `data-verification.md` is approved (the approval is bound to its SHA-256).
{% for note in llm_notes %}
- Check: {{ note }}
{% endfor %}

## 2. Freeze writes on the source

- Put the applications into maintenance mode or stop writers.
{% if databases %}
- PostgreSQL is copied with `pg_dump`/`pg_restore` (point in time): writes made after
  the dump started are not on STACKIT. Keep writes frozen, or re-run
  `migrate data {{ plan.run_id }} --execute` inside the window.
{% endif %}

## 3. Final sync (automated by the approved cutover)

{% for b in buckets if b.status.value == "copied" %}
- `{{ b.source }}` → `{{ b.target }}`: final `rclone copy` (no deletes).
{% endfor %}
{% for b in buckets if b.status.value == "skipped" %}
- `{{ b.source }}`: **not migrated**: {{ b.error }}
{% endfor %}

## 4. Switch the applications

{% for db in databases %}
- {{ db.name }}: point connection strings to the STACKIT instance
  ({% if db.terraform_type == "stackit_postgresflex_instance" %}`terraform output {{ db.tf }}_host`, `{{ db.tf }}_port`{% else %}`terraform output {{ db.tf }}_host`{% endif %}; passwords from the sensitive outputs, never from this file).
{% endfor %}
{% if buckets %}
- Object storage: endpoint `https://object.storage.eu01.onstackit.cloud`, region `eu01`, same bucket names; keys from the sensitive Terraform outputs.
{% endif %}
{% for lb in load_balancers %}
- DNS: point the application hostname of `{{ lb.name }}` to `terraform output {{ lb.tf }}_address` (lower the TTL a day before).
{% endfor %}

## 5. Verify

- Smoke-test the application end to end.
- Start monitoring: `migrate monitor {{ plan.run_id }} --interval 60`.

## 6. Rollback

- Switch DNS and connection strings back to AWS. Nothing on AWS was changed or deleted.
- Data written on STACKIT after the switch must be reconciled manually.

## 7. Decommissioning

Deleting source resources is **out of scope** for this system and must follow
the client's own change process after a stabilisation period.
